<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Bitumen_KorvethSource.xml         UtinniPatches — SUMP_WALKWAYS_1 /
                                         SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 reconciliation

  Both items' own headers flagged the SAME gap: RUT_Bitumen
  (Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RUT_Bitumen.xml, SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1) shipped with
  no recipeMaker and no harvest job, "tradeable/debug-spawnable in the
  meantime" — its own header explicitly named the korveth plant's harvest
  as the exact real source it was waiting for, not yet built at the time.

  SUMP_FLORA_ROSTER_1 has since shipped that plant — but as a SEPARATE
  ThingDef, RM_KorvethPitch (RM_TheSump, mandrake.rm.thesump), not literally
  RUT_Bitumen itself: RM tier may not depend on RUT tier (the free mod must
  stand rich alone, Q11a), so the korveth's own harvest could never BE this
  campaign-tier good directly. The correct join, same shape this repo's own
  RUT_TarVault.xml already uses for a different Sump good (MayRequire=
  "mandrake.rm.thesump" wherever this mod references a RM_TheSump defName):
  a real recipe refining the free mod's raw pitch into this campaign's own
  engineered building material — "solid black pitch, rendered from raw tar
  until it sets hard" (RUT_Bitumen's own description) is quite literally
  what a bench recipe on top of "a hard black nodule of concentrated
  bitumen" (RM_KorvethPitch's own description) already reads as.

  PatchOperationConditional (silent no-op if RM_TheSump is ever absent,
  matching WildAnimals_Sump.xml's own idiom) wrapping a
  PatchOperationSequence — one Add for recipeMaker+costList onto the
  ThingDef itself, a second Add for WorkToMake onto its existing
  <statBases> (RUT_Bitumen.xml's own file is left untouched; this is an
  isolated patch, per this repo's own "correctness outranks seat ownership"
  practice of fixing a flagged gap without editing another pass's file
  directly where a patch does the same job more safely). productCount 1
  (a straight refine, not the deliberately-generous 4:1 SUMP_GASLIGHT_1
  ruling gave the solvent) off 2 pitch — RUT_Bitumen's own MarketValue (1.8)
  sits below 2x RM_KorvethPitch's (1.2), so refining costs real value, same
  as any vanilla smelting step. WorkToMake 200, same order of magnitude
  RUT_WeakTarSolvent's own 150 uses for a comparable bench conversion.

  RUT_Bitumen is still tradeable/debug-spawnable with no korveth pitch on
  hand — this patch adds a real production path, it does not remove the
  existing placeholder-sourcing posture for a colony without RM_TheSump's
  korveth crop established yet.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.thesump">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Bitumen"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Bitumen"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <recipeMaker>
              <recipeUsers>
                <li>TableMachining</li>
              </recipeUsers>
              <workSpeedStat>GeneralLaborSpeed</workSpeedStat>
              <workSkill>Crafting</workSkill>
              <displayPriority>425</displayPriority>
              <productCount>1</productCount>
            </recipeMaker>
            <costList>
              <RM_KorvethPitch>2</RM_KorvethPitch>
            </costList>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_Bitumen"]/statBases</xpath>
          <value>
            <WorkToMake>200</WorkToMake>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
